# Keep the build context lean and the build deterministic.
#
# _site and .jekyll-cache are the two that matter: `COPY . /Ephesus` was
# shipping a previously built _site and a stale incremental cache into the
# image, so a cached layer could serve output that did not match the source
# that layer was built from. The Dockerfile rebuilds both anyway.
.git
.github
.jekyll-cache
_site
node_modules
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.log
